    "question": "A train takes 4 hours to reach a destination at a speed of 50 miles per hour. How long would it take if it traveled at 100 miles per hour instead?",
    "question_sha256": "08eefb41029c2a599063cdf21b58d7423224ffc3843e898f00aea78940c7a5bb",
    "responses": [
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-7319:rich",
        "raw_call_sha256": "99696da2be5c72317ddb6619de8760462dabb2c070d6adc4c8f8eba1963caf0f",
        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "A train takes 4 hours to reach a destination at a speed of 50 miles per hour. How long would it take if it traveled at 100 miles per hour instead?",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "4da0a938d990a29abb8bb467244b8713896da77efae61732b06ab532a151835f",
        "target": "Given:\n- Speed at first journey = 50 miles per hour\n- Time for first journey = 4 hours\n\nFirst, calculate the distance to the destination:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 50 \\, \\text{miles/hour} \\times 4 \\, \\text{hours} = 200 \\, \\text{miles} \\]\n\nNow, for the second journey at 100 miles per hour, calculate the time:\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} = \\frac{200 \\, \\text{miles}}{100 \\, \\text{miles/hour}} = 2 \\, \\text{hours} \\]\n\nFINAL: 2",
        "target_sha256": "274790b22913c0a1923355b6da54b2720e10d89eac1705b7368ae25e566264d5"
      },
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-7319:new_record",
        "raw_call_sha256": "f44c1e6e8b31cfe3bf8eed3cb71d8e4c1bda94b6602ee247ff5a04f5c3f6d606",
