{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"775","question_sha256":"6e4fd342cb9219719210074ec2fc9dfc8d4555d1f4c8d960ee11610a1119d947","reason":"Main-job daily pay is 16×8=128 and part-time daily pay is 13.5×2=27. Thus daily pay is 128+27=155, and 155×5=775, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3957"},{"independent_answer":"7 if “1/3 times longer” means one-third longer; 4 if it means one-third as long","question_sha256":"467b14c3e5019f8489f95591459dc973b5e24f79ee6dd804c2cb649336fde409","reason":"Under the usual intended reading of one-third longer, Zendaya takes 6+(6/3)=8 hours and the average is (6+8)/2=7. However, “1/3 times longer” is linguistically questionable and can be read as one-third as long, giving Zendaya 2 hours and an average of 4, so the gold is not unambiguous.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6104"},{"independent_answer":"19","question_sha256":"7f8e2b08b482710b12b699fb7471c8f2cdafb63ee181a67f9e8afd6be73bc7d4","reason":"Washington-to-Idaho time is 640/80=8 hours, and Idaho-to-Nevada time is 550/50=11 hours. The total is 8+11=19 hours, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4681"},{"independent_answer":"7","question_sha256":"7fd774d1a87f135b917cc931148795c9ff9c8d6cde78eb9de0576a5ca175aa0a","reason":"Chris earns 8×9=72 dollars. His purchases cost 60+5=65 dollars, leaving 72−65=7 dollars, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-2846"},{"independent_answer":"1","question_sha256":"b7dbcb8604f389df24db41e2cdf62aeec68f89ba6bb6c554bcacf24dfc220195","reason":"The downhill trail takes 20/5=4 hours. The uphill trail takes 12/3=4 hours of hiking plus a 1-hour break, totaling 5 hours. The faster hike is 5−4=1 hour faster, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5410"},{"independent_answer":"52","question_sha256":"fe42f54b35c63c784d1eb13f580a6b0183dbb361f5c0a85b9f18d26e407cf45f","reason":"The second job pays 12×9=108 dollars. Subtracting this from total wages gives 160−108=52 dolla